SOAPBOX: For the contest, I operated the amazing station owned by Paul, 
SOAPBOX: W1IMD, controlling the Flex 8600 with a Maestro from my home in 
SOAPBOX: Colorado. It was a lot of fun. Last year I did the contest in 
SOAPBOX: France with a Yaesu FT-891 and an EFHW off the apartment balcony. 
SOAPBOX: It is different from this side of the Atlantic! 
 
80 meters was 
SOAPBOX: active for the first hour, and then went to 40m, and when those 
SOAPBOX: went quiet, I was on 20m for a stretch. Sunday was a mix of all 
SOAPBOX: the bands, wrapping up with 10m at the end. I worked most of the 
SOAPBOX: contest, with just a few hours of off time. 
 
 It was fun to 
SOAPBOX: have QSOs with mes amis francais! 
 
Many thanks to W1IMD.
